& [Purpose]
  + bind one proposed inner Cantor session host and process identity to one exact validated NHC-01 outer envelope
  + make parent-child lineage deterministic inspectable and reusable without asserting operating-system ancestry liveness launch consent custody or model authority

& [Profiles]
  + [NHIL-001] request profile is cantor-nested-inner-process-lineage-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-nested-inner-process-lineage-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-nested-inner-process-lineage-verification/0.1
  + [NHIL-002] strict machine forms are compact UTF-8 JSON denying unknown duplicate or trailing properties and bounded to 1048576 bytes depth 24 fields 256 text 1024 and evidence 32

& [ParentBinding]
  + [NHIL-003] the complete supplied NHC-01 envelope must validate against its own unchanged request before any child result exists
  + [NHIL-004] parent session outer-host and outer-process anchors exactly equal the validated NHC-01 request and parent envelope digest exactly equals the supplied envelope
  + [NHIL-005] the NHC-01 lifecycle remains proposed_identity_only and its physical_process_not_observed model_not_loaded and provider_not_contacted truths remain conserved

& [InnerBinding]
  + [NHIL-006] lineage inner-session inner-Cantor and inner-process identities are nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing SemanticIds distinct from one another and every NHC-01 operational identity
  + [NHIL-007] inner binding kind is inner_cantor declared state is declared_unobserved and implementation plus configuration identities are SHA256 values
  + [NHIL-008] lineage relationship is proposed_parent_child_unobserved depth is exactly one and child ordinal is exactly one

& [Request]
  + [NHIL-009] one through 32 unique evidence references are required and unresolved account is exactly parent_process_not_observed child_process_not_observed child_not_launched lineage_not_observed model_not_admitted and provider_not_contacted
  + [NHIL-010] request nonauthority states supplied identity correspondence does not establish physical ancestry launch model custody attention workspace persistence remote or effect authority
  + [NHIL-011] request digest is domain-separated SHA256 over deterministic JSON with only its own digest blanked

& [Envelope]
  + [NHIL-012] compilation emits proposed_lineage_only lifecycle lineage_correspondence_only authority the complete unchanged request exact parent and request digests ten fixed capability denials lineage digest and envelope digest
  + [NHIL-013] denials are process_observation process_launch model_admission model_load provider_call shared_attention persistence workspace_mutation external_effect and remote_access
  + [NHIL-014] lineage and envelope digests are independently domain separated deterministic and self excluding

& [Verification]
  + [NHIL-015] verification revalidates outer and child forms exact correspondence identities bounds unresolved truths denials nonauthority lifecycle authority and every digest before reporting seven identities ten denials six unresolved truths and all effect counts zero
  + [NHIL-016] equal valid requests compile byte identically and retained evidence independently replays exact request envelope verification and manifest twice
  + [NHIL-017] profile unknown duplicate trailing oversize identity collision parent substitution state relationship depth ordinal digest evidence unresolved denial authority lifecycle request or envelope mutation fails closed with typed faults and no partial output
  + [NHIL-018] production code performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model MCP Git workspace persistence remote deployment cleanup or external effect action

& [Acceptance]
  + [NHIL-A01] source audit delineation data dual threat seven-fold canonical explosion justification solution plan matrix phase lock proof review and satisfaction signature agree exactly
  + [NHIL-A02] safe Rust module exports closed forms validation compilation digests and strict machine-form functions using existing dependencies only
  + [NHIL-A03] focused positive deterministic and adversarial tests plus two bounded CLIs retained evidence and an independent verifier pass debug and overflow-checked release
  + [NHIL-A04] exact workspace debug release warnings-denied Clippy format evidence graph attribution and remote-equal publication gates pass
  + [NHIL-A05] NHC-03 model identity NHC-04 launch NHC-05 custody NHC-06 attention live provider remote deployment and every effect remain separately governed

& [Invalidation]
  + source predecessor profile outer-envelope validation identity relation state bound evidence unresolved denial authority lifecycle digest effect dependency requirement support or attribution drift
